{"id": 108013, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 1-day-old girl is evaluated in the newborn nursery due to swollen hands and feet.\u00a0 She was born at term via cesarean delivery.\u00a0 The newborn's vital signs are normal.\u00a0 Examination is significant for a short, webbed neck; dysplastic nails; and bilateral, nonpitting carpal and pedal edema.\u00a0 Ultrasound examination of the abdomen reveals a horseshoe kidney.\u00a0 Which of the following is the most likely cause of this infant's edema?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Excessive urinary sodium retention"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Impaired left ventricle contractility"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Increased capillary permeability"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Increased urinary loss of protein"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Lymphatic network dysgenesis"}], "correctAnswer": "E", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_t67525\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">E</mark>dema</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Mechanism</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Examples</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Characteristics</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</strong><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> Capillary hydrostatic pressure</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Heart failure</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Glomerulonephritis, renal failure</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Venous obstruction/insufficiency</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Pitting</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Symmetric (eg, systemic conditions) or asymmetric (eg, DVT)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dependent</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u2193</strong><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> Capillary oncotic pressure </strong>(hypoalbuminemia)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Protein loss (eg, nephrotic syndrome)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Decreased protein synthesis (eg, cirrhosis, malnutrition)</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</strong><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> Capillary permeability</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Burns, sepsis</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Allergic reactions</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hereditary angioedema</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nonpitting (lymphedema may initially be pitting)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Usually asymmetric</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nondependent* or dependent**</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Lymphatic obstruction</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Malignancy</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Congenital lymphedema</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">*Edema is nondependent with increased capillary permeability.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">**Edema is dependent with lymphatic obstruction.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">DVT</strong> = deep venous thrombosis.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This newborn has edema involving the hands and feet.\u00a0 Edema develops due to accumulation of fluid in the interstitial space.\u00a0 It can be categorized as pitting (ie, makes a physical indentation with applied pressure) or nonpitting.</p><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Pitting edema typically results when there is increased fluid extravasation into the interstitial space.\u00a0 Common causes include increased capillary hydrostatic pressure (eg, right-sided heart failure, venous thrombosis) and decreased intravascular oncotic pressure (eg, nephrotic-range proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia in cirrhosis) <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>.</p></li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nonpitting edema</strong>\u00a0occurs when there is impaired drainage of excess interstitial water due to lymphatic obstruction (eg, malignancy, congenital hypoplasia) or accumulation of water-binding mucopolysaccharides in the interstitial space (ie, pretibial myxedema in hypothyroidism).\u00a0 Increased capillary permeability (eg, angioedema) also characteristically causes nonpitting due to rapid extravasation of protein-rich fluid that overwhelms the normal drainage pathways <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>.</p></li></ul><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">In this case, the patient has nonpitting edema in addition to a webbed neck, nail dysplasia, and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">horseshoe kidney</strong>, a constellation of findings that is characteristic of <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-ihtyfvioj67chs7hntvrrvi1\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-ihtyfvioj67chs7hntvrrvi1\">Turner syndrome</a> (TS).\u00a0 Swelling occurs in more than half of patients with TS and is due to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">lymphatic network dysgenesis</strong> causing <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-i5p1ekf3epmmr9vuprqjtqt5\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-i5p1ekf3epmmr9vuprqjtqt5\">congenital lymphedema</a>.\u00a0 Poor lymph absorption leads to the accumulation of fluid in the interstitial space of the hands and feet.\u00a0 Impaired drainage of cervical lymph results in formation of a <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">webbed neck</strong> (ie, short neck with loose skin), and severe obstruction of lymphatic vessels can result in <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-c190j1n34dculb41fv8cmas9\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-c190j1n34dculb41fv8cmas9\">cystic hygroma</a> and hydrops fetalis.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Sodium (and therefore fluid) retention occurs with kidney failure and causes increased capillary hydrostatic pressure and edema that is pitting, in contrast to this patient's nonpitting edema.\u00a0 In addition, although patients with TS are predisposed to horseshoe kidney, renal function is usually normal.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Impaired left ventricle contractility initially causes left-sided heart failure and presents with signs of pulmonary edema, such as increased work of breathing (eg, tachypnea), hypoxia, and crackles (findings not seen in this patient).\u00a0 Over time, increased pulmonary pressure can cause increased central venous pressure and lead to right-sided heart failure, but edema would be pitting, unlike the edema in this patient.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Nonpitting edema often develops due to lymphatic outflow obstruction (eg, malignancy, congenital malformation).\u00a0 Congenital lymphedema due to lymphatic network dysgenesis\u00a0is common in Turner syndrome, which is also characteristically associated with webbed neck, horseshoe kidney, and nail dysplasia.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Nonpitting edema often develops due to lymphatic outflow obstruction (eg, malignancy, congenital malformation).  Congenital lymphedema due to lymphatic network dysgenesis is common in Turner syndrome, which is also characteristically associated with webbed neck, horseshoe kidney, and nail dysplasia.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200